{
  "subtype": "focus_inference",
  "implied_focus": "The nature and provenance of procured assets underlying the travel-expense records (asset acquisition/lifecycle profiling)",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "asset_category",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Classifies what kind of asset the expense represents -- a core facet of an asset-centric focus."
    },
    {
      "name": "creation_mode",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Describes how the record/asset entry was generated (automated vs manual), a provenance facet of asset acquisition."
    },
    {
      "name": "business_purpose",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Ties each asset to why it was acquired; coheres with an acquisition-purpose framing."
    },
    {
      "name": "asset_specificity",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Granularity of asset identification (named model vs generic vs service) -- an attribute of the asset concept."
    },
    {
      "name": "department_span",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "Essentially restates the existing department column; a spend/owner dimension, only loosely about the asset focus."
    },
    {
      "name": "processing_lag_signal",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "Derived timing metric from processed vs opened dates; a data-quality/process facet, not an asset attribute."
    },
    {
      "name": "source_tracking_completeness",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "Bare presence/absence flag on source_id -- a generic data-completeness check, not asset-focused."
    },
    {
      "name": "asset_lifecycle_stage",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Places the asset in acquisition/registration/maintenance stages -- a genuine lifecycle facet of the asset focus."
    }
  ],
  "focus_coherence": 0.55,
  "structure_quality": 0.55,
  "focus_actionability": 0.5,
  "rationale": "A majority of columns (asset_category, asset_specificity, asset_lifecycle_stage, creation_mode, business_purpose) do centre on a coherent asset-acquisition/provenance concept, so an implied focus is inferable and the set is not a pure grab-bag. However, coherence is diluted by three off-theme additions: department_span merely restates an existing column, while processing_lag_signal and source_tracking_completeness are generic process/data-quality flags that pull toward a different (data-hygiene) axis. Structurally the asset facets form a reasonable multi-faceted decomposition (type, specificity, lifecycle, purpose, provenance), but the mixing of asset facets with completeness/timing signals weakens it as a clean predictor/attribute set. The focus is somewhat actionable -- an analyst could investigate what assets drive travel expenses and how they are procured -- but there is notable tension because the operator reframed 'travel-expense records' as an asset-procurement problem, which may not match the spend/cost focus the query most naturally invites, capping actionability."
}

